---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import EmailCaptureForm from '../components/EmailCaptureForm.tsx';

const capabilities = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Frame', body: 'Clarifies the actual mandate, why the decision is active and what a good outcome means before moving to advice.' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Inspect', body: 'Separates GIVEN, DERIVED, INFERRED and UNKNOWN, then exposes contradictions, inherited constraints and load-bearing assumptions.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Test', body: 'Forms a working view, asks what evidence could change it and keeps unresolved uncertainty visible instead of smoothing it away.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Compare', body: 'Develops genuinely relevant options and tests them against criteria established for the decision rather than the preferred answer.' },
  { n: '05', name: 'Decide', body: 'Makes the call when the evidence permits. When it does not, it specifies the next evidence-producing decision and what result would change the call.' },
  { n: '06', name: 'Execute', body: 'Turns the decision into proportionate actions, ownership, measures, evidence thresholds and review conditions.' },
];
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="The Decision Frame | A portable decision system for AI"
  description="The free GreenSquare Decision Frame gives a capable AI model a disciplined method to interrogate a business decision, inspect evidence, compare options and make a traceable call."
  current="frame"
>
  <section class="v-section v-off hero">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow v-reveal">
      <h1 class="v-display">Give it the problem. It works out what to ask next.</h1>
      <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">
        The Decision Frame turns a capable AI model into a disciplined thinking partner. It clarifies the mandate,
        interrogates evidence and assumptions, compares relevant options, makes the call when possible and turns it
        into action.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="#get-it">Get the free Decision Frame</a>
        <a class="v-btn v-btn--grey" href="#how-it-works">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow v-reveal">
      <h2 class="v-h2">Ordinary AI can answer the wrong decision very well.</h2>
      <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
        A model will often accept the question, constraints and options it is given. The Decision Frame changes what
        happens before the answer. It controls how the model interrogates the situation, advances the reasoning and
        decides whether the evidence is strong enough to make the call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-fill">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h2 class="v-h2">A decision process that adapts to the problem.</h2>
      <div class="v-caplist">
        {capabilities.map((item, index) => (
          <div class={`v-caprow v-reveal${index > 0 ? ` d${Math.min(index, 3)}` : ''}`}>
            <span class="v-index">State {item.n}</span>
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p class="v-small v-cap-body">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-top">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">One file. One conversation. No prompt engineering.</h2>
        <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
          Download the Decision Frame, upload it to a capable AI model and give it the decision or business problem.
          It should explain the method briefly, then begin with one focused question and adapt from there.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-readout">
          <div class="v-readout__bar"><span class="v-readout__dot"></span> How to use it</div>
          <div class="v-readout__body">
            <ul class="v-spec__list">
              <li><span class="n">1</span> Download the file</li>
              <li><span class="n">2</span> Upload it to your AI</li>
              <li><span class="n">3</span> Give it the problem</li>
              <li><span class="n">4</span> Answer one focused question at a time</li>
              <li><span class="n">5</span> Receive a traceable decision and execution path</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-green">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow v-reveal">
      <p class="v-quote">The moment to look for is simple: it knew what to ask next.</p>
      <p class="v-small" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); max-width: 70ch;">
        This describes the intended experience, not a quantified performance claim. The launch compatibility note
        will reflect the model versions actually tested for the locked release.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow">
      <h2 class="v-h2">The output shows the state of the decision.</h2>
      <div class="v-card v-reveal" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">
        <ul class="v-leadlist">
          <li><strong>The mandate.</strong> What is actually being decided, why it is active and what success means.</li>
          <li><strong>The evidence state.</strong> What is GIVEN, DERIVED, INFERRED and still UNKNOWN.</li>
          <li><strong>The working view.</strong> The hypothesis, alternatives and assumption carrying the most risk.</li>
          <li><strong>The options and scorecard.</strong> Relevant paths compared against the same decision criteria.</li>
          <li><strong>The recommendation.</strong> The call, confidence, accepted trade-offs and what would change it.</li>
          <li><strong>The execution path.</strong> The next action, owner, measures, evidence thresholds and review trigger.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-green" id="get-it">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-top">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">Put a stronger judgement process behind your next decision.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-5);">
          Enter your email and confirm the address. Decision Frame V2 will arrive immediately after confirmation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-card">
          <EmailCaptureForm client:visible buttonLabel="Email me the Decision Frame" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 5rem); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--v-4); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-8); }
</style>
